From 73dd03b4a282b2755f5bde37e4e0cb81e4a81dd8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: howl <howeili@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 10:19:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] sm89: keep the ratio-1/2 compressed KV in the reference's FP4
 (SGLANG_SM89_FP4_COMPRESSED_KV)

DeepSeek-V4.1 rounds its ratio-1/2 compressed latents to e2m1 with an e4m3 scale per 16
after RoPE (fp4_act_quant in the checkpoint's model.py); SGLang has that layout (V41_FP4,
288 B a token). On SM89 the pool kept them in the V4 584-byte layout instead (e4m3 per 64,
RoPE part in bf16): a second rounding of values already on the fp4 grid.

With SGLANG_SM89_FP4_COMPRESSED_KV=1, on compute capability 8.9 only:
- the pool gives the ratio-1/2 caches V41_FP4 next to the V4 main cache, and the pair is
  valid; another GPU that keeps the V4 main cache refuses to start (SM100 already has
  V41_FP4), and so does SGLANG_DSV4_KV_LAYOUT=v4 with an fp8 compressed layout;
- the store writes the e2m1 codes with the software helpers ROCm uses (SM89 has no
  cvt.rn.satfinite.e2m1x2); other GPUs keep the hardware conversion;
- the dual-scope decode kernels, unsplit and split-K, read the 288-byte rows through
  sm89_fp4_tile.fp4_tile in a copy of _process_kv_block_aggressive: the same dots and
  folds on the same shapes, only the tiles load differently. e2m1 x e4m3 is exact in bf16;
- the portable separate-scope path refuses these rows.
Off, nothing changes: the kernels take EXTRA_FP4=False, a constexpr.

Checked by howl9003 on an RTX 4080 SUPER, on their SM89 build (SGLang 5d8e90a0, the
unsplit kernel):
- the store against fp4_act_quant after RoPE: 0 of 151,009,280 values differ;
- the reader against SGLang's dequantization: 0 of 4,521,984; the attention against a
  twin reading the same values as bf16 rows: 0 of 3,000 calls; off, the kernels against
  the files before: 0 of 600 calls; no spills;
- panel KL against the reference 0.01106 -> 0.01098, NLL paired by conversation -0.00056
  (SE 0.00084); decode flat, 35K prefill +0.8%.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
